Package: stratsampling
Title: Stratified Sampling for Model-Assisted Treatment Effect Estimation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Reagan", "Mozer", email = "rmozer@bentley.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1302-0503")),
    person("Nicole", "Pashley", role = "aut"),
    person("Luke", "Miratrix", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Tools for stratified sampling designs that leverage surrogate
    scores (e.g., machine learning predictions) to efficiently estimate
    treatment effects when human coding is expensive. Provides functions for
    creating and evaluating candidate stratifications, drawing stratified
    samples, and computing model-assisted estimators that combine surrogate
    predictions with a bias-corrected adjustment from a coded subsample.
    Also includes power analysis tools and simulation utilities for
    comparing sampling designs. Methods are described in Mozer, Pashley,
    and Miratrix (2026).
